CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model data:observe_data --nondet-volatile-write-model cmd:observe_cmd --mmio-weak
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
data committed before GO: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
Cross-function deferral: the helper write_data posts the write to the data
register and returns without a barrier. Because posted writes have static
lifetime, the write can be delayed past the function return and observed after
the command in main, so the ordering assertion fails. A model that flushed at
the helper's return would miss this bug.
